<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Armour acquisition (docs/features/armour-acquisition.md). Hand-edited; validated at load by
  ArmourAcquisitionConfigProvider (a bad value reverts to its compiled default with a warning in
  the TAOM log). Read once per process: changes need a full Bannerlord restart.

  The class of every armour piece comes from the GENERATED armour_classes.xml beside this file.
  This file holds the decisions around it.

  enabled            default for the master switch when MCM is not loaded; with MCM, the
                     "Enable Armour Acquisition" toggle decides, from the next game load.

  <Gate>             the armoury level a town needs (its Barracks level, plus a visiting master
                     armourer's bonus), 0 to 3, heavy <= elite <= lord. At that level the town's
                     market may stock the class and its armoury may upgrade a piece into it (Mike,
                     2026-09-27: heavy 1, elite and heavy 2, lord and all 3). Named pieces are
                     never sold.

  <Upgrades>         what turning a piece into its next class costs, one <Upgrade> per class the
                     piece becomes (medium, heavy, elite, lord):
                       gold               flat gold, 0 to 1,000,000
                       value_share        0 to 1: this share of the value the piece gains is
                                          added to the gold
                       special_resource   0 to 10,000 of the player's kingdom special resource
                                          (Castar, Gems, War Spoils ...); waived when the
                                          kingdom has none
                       <Material>         item id and count (1 to 999) taken from the party
                     When this element is present it lists every recipe; a class with no recipe
                     cannot be upgraded into.

  <NamedWeapons>     hero weapon and shield ids that are never sold or looted (Mike: seventeen on
                     2026-09-27; Tuor's heirloom axes, Galadriel's sword and the seven Noldor
                     swords on 2026-09-28). The ladder's weapon rung awards the named weapons
                     (Mike, 2026-09-28); the two shields have no route yet.

  <LordEvent>        after a battle your side wins against an enemy lord: the chance (0 to 1)
                     of finding his household's lord harness, the cooldown in days, and the
                     relation (0 to 100) gained with him for leaving it.

  <VisitingArmourer> each day, the chance (0 to 1) that a master armourer visits one town, how
                     many days (1 to 365) he stays, and the armoury levels (0 to 3) he adds.

  <LordsLadder>      the lord's gear ladder (#693): one <Step> per rung, climbed in the order listed.
                     slot is hands, legs, shoulders, head, body or weapon (each once); quest names
                     its career-quest definition in taom_career_quests.xml, whose objectives are the
                     rung's deeds; materials (1 to 999) is how many lord's materials complete the
                     rung instead. count_knockouts: whether an enemy the hero knocks out counts as
                     struck down, as well as one killed. A rung's piece is claimed at an armoury of
                     the lord level: the culture's lord pieces for the slot, else its best elite
                     piece there, else its best heavy piece, else any culture's lord pieces for the
                     slot. A save keeps which slots each hero has claimed and which are done, so after
                     a reorder or a removed <Step> every hero resumes at their first unclaimed rung, and
                     a done rung stays done in its own slot.

  <LordsMaterials>   the chance (0 to 1) that a battle won yields lord's materials: base_chance,
                     plus chance_per_ten_kills for every ten enemies the hero struck down in it, up
                     to max_chance; and how many units (1 to 99, min_units to max_units) a find
                     holds. One <Material> per culture: the item it finds and hands in
                     (taom_lords_materials.xml). A culture with none uses its armour donor's
                     (culture_marketplace_config.xml, armour_from). When present it lists them all;
                     a section that yields no valid row keeps the compiled defaults.

  <LadderWeapons>    the weapons the weapon rung offers, one <Weapon> per choice, by culture: a
                     culture's named weapons where it has them, else a pick (Mike, 2026-09-28). A
                     culture with none uses its armour donor's. When present it lists them all;
                     a section that yields no valid row keeps the compiled defaults.

  <LadderPieces>     optional: named armour pieces an armour rung offers before its ordinary choices,
                     one <Piece culture slot item> per piece (slot is hands, legs, shoulders, head or
                     body; a weapon belongs in <LadderWeapons>). Looked up for the hero's own culture
                     only, never its armour donor's, and a piece the Armory does not load is skipped.
                     Meant for a named piece (armour_classes.xml) that is never sold, so the ladder is
                     its only route (Mike, 2026-10-08). Absent or empty: no rung gets a named piece.
-->
<ArmourAcquisition enabled="true">
  <Gate heavy="1" elite="2" lord="3" />

  <Upgrades>
    <Upgrade target="medium" gold="150" value_share="0.25">
      <Material item="ironIngot2" count="3" />
      <Material item="ironIngot1" count="2" />
    </Upgrade>
    <Upgrade target="heavy" gold="500" value_share="0.35">
      <Material item="ironIngot4" count="3" />
      <Material item="ironIngot3" count="4" />
    </Upgrade>
    <Upgrade target="elite" gold="1500" value_share="0.5">
      <Material item="ironIngot5" count="4" />
      <Material item="ironIngot4" count="3" />
    </Upgrade>
    <Upgrade target="lord" gold="3000" value_share="0.5" special_resource="150">
      <Material item="ironIngot6" count="6" />
    </Upgrade>
  </Upgrades>

  <NamedWeapons>
